<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husam al-Din Timurtash</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1122–1154</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Husam al-Din Timurtash was the Artuqid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a> from 1122 to 1154, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilghazi">Ilghazi</a>. He briefly held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> after his father's death, released the captive King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-ii-of-jerusalem">Baldwin II of Jerusalem</a> for a ransom in 1124, and kept Mardin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a> by balancing between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zengid-dynasty">Zengids</a> and other neighbouring powers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/husam-al-din-timurtash.jpg" alt="Husam al-Din Timurtash" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artuqids_(Mardin)._Husam_al-Din_Timurtash._AH_516-547_AD_1122-1152._Diademed,_Seleukid-style_bust_right._Name_and_titles_of_Timurtash_in_four_lines_and_in_margins.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
